# Web export (Godot must be available)

After any completed change that affects gameplay, UI, version, or shipped assets:

1. Run `bash tools/export-web.sh` (it installs Godot 4.3 + templates if missing, then exports).
2. Commit the updated `index.html`, `index.js`, `index.wasm` (if changed), `index.pck`, and the versioned `index-<ver>.pck` produced by the script.
3. Push so GitHub Pages serves the new pack. The script cache-busts via `mainPack: index-<version>.pck` so browsers do not keep showing an old title-menu version.

Do **not** claim a version bump is live until the web export has been rebuilt and pushed.

If `godot` is missing mid-session, run `bash tools/ensure-godot.sh` first.
